    "_comentario": "How the assistant's tool search splits and normalizes words (src/app/mcp/McpIndice.cpp). French: the imperative («affiche», «coupe», «lance») is the infinitive minus its last letter, so «infinitivo» (er, ir, re) lets «afficher» find «affiche…» and the prefix match does the rest; there is no «imperativo». Attached pronouns go with a hyphen («affiche-moi»), which already splits, so no «pegados»; the apostrophe splits too («l'écran» → l, ecran), hence the elided l, d, j, m, t, s, qu in «vacias». Not in «vacias» because they tell what is asked: ne, n, pas, plus, tout, tous, toutes, rien, stop, suivant, précédent, arrêt, oui, non, sur, sous, haut, bas, avant, après, entrée, sortie. See docs/desarrollo/I18N.md, «Perfil del idioma: buscador».",
